        "content": "Zero coverage on the actual security boundary of the app.\n\n**Gaps:**\n- `requireReviewer()` throws when `isAuthenticated` is false\n- `requireReviewer()` throws when `userId` is falsy even if `isAuthenticated` is true (defensive double-check — currently unverified this branch is reachable/correct)\n- `requireReviewer()` returns `{ userId, label }` built via `reviewerLabel` when authenticated\n- `getReviewer()` returns `null` when unauthenticated (and does **not** call `currentUser()` — verify no wasted call)\n- `getReviewer()` delegates to `requireReviewer()` when authenticated\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/auth.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\", () => ({\n  auth: vi.fn(),\n  currentUser: vi.fn(),\n}));\n\ndescribe(\"requireReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"throws when not authenticated\", async () => {\n    const { auth } = await import(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\");\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false, userId: null } as any);\n    const { requireReviewer } = await import(\"./auth\");\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow(/No authenticated reviewer/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns userId and label when authenticated\", async () => {\n    const { auth, currentUser } = await import(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\");\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"uid_1\" } as any);\n    vi.mocked(currentUser).mockResolvedValue({ username: \"j.rao\" } as any);\n    const { requireReviewer } = await import(\"./auth\");\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"uid_1\", label: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when unauthenticated, without calling currentUser\", async () => {\n    const { auth, currentUser } = await import(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\");\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false } as any);\n    const { getReviewer } = await import(\"./auth\");\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toBeNull();\n    expect(currentUser).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "3. Route protection — `proxy.ts` (critical, zero coverage)",
        "content": "\nThis is the sole access-control gate for an internal tool handling org charts and audit mutations. No test verifies the matcher logic.\n\n**Gaps — integration-level, needs Playwright or a Next.js middleware test harness:**\n- `/` is public (no redirect to sign-in)\n- `/sign-in` and `/sign-in/anything` are public\n- `/sign-up` and nested routes are public\n- Any other route (e.g. `/sources`, `/api/anything`) redirects unauthenticated requests\n- Static assets matched by the negative-lookahead regex are *not* intercepted (e.g. `/logo.svg`, `/foo.css`)\n- `/api/*` and `/trpc/*` are protected even though they'd otherwise be excluded by the first matcher pattern\n\n```ts\n// e2e/proxy.spec.ts (Playwright)\nimport { test, expect } from \"@playwright/test\";\n\ntest(\"unauthenticated user is redirected off a protected console route\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.goto(\"/sources\");\n  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/sign-in/);\n});\n\ntest(\"landing page is reachable without auth\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.goto(\"/\");\n  await expect(page).not.toHaveURL(/sign-in/);\n});\n\ntest(\"sign-in route itself does not redirect\", async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.goto(\"/sign-in\");\n  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/sign-in/);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "4. Components — currently zero rendered/interaction tests",
        "content": "\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "`components/severity-mark.tsx`",
        "content": "Encodes AGENTS.md's \"no color\" severity rule — a regression here is a compliance bug, not just cosmetic.\n\n```ts\n// components/severity-mark.test.tsx\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { SeverityMark } from \"./severity-mark\";\n\ndescribe(\"SeverityMark\", () => {\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4] as const)(\"always renders the severity word alongside the mark for level %d\", (sev) => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={sev} />);\n    // The mark must never be the only signal — assert label text is present.\n    expect(screen.getByText(/./)).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "`components/sources/source-table.tsx`",
        "content": "No test on the render logic that maps `Source[]` → rows.\n\n**Gaps:** empty array renders header-only (no crash), a row renders correct kind/side lookups, `objects` array joins with `, `, multiple sources render distinct `key`s without React warnings.\n\n```ts\n// components/sources/source-table.test.tsx\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { SourceTable } from \"./source-table\";\n\nconst source = {\n  id: \"1\", name: \"SFDC\", kind: \"salesforce\" as const,\n  config: { objects: [\"Account\", \"Contact\"] }, createdAt: new Date(),\n};\n\ndescribe(\"SourceTable\", () => {\n  it(\"renders no rows for an empty list\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[]} />);\n    expect(screen.queryByRole(\"row\")).toBeTruthy(); // header row only\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders kind label, side, and joined objects for a source\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[source]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Salesforce\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"crm\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Account, Contact\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "`components/ui/button.tsx`",
        "content": "No test that variant/size class combinations resolve correctly, or that `asChild` actually renders the child element instead of a `<button>`.\n\n```ts\n// components/ui/button.test.tsx\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { Button } from \"./button\";\n\ndescribe(\"Button\", () => {\n  it(\"renders a native button by default\", () => {\n    render(<Button>Go</Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Go\" })).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"respects disabled state\", () => {\n    render(<Button disabled>Go</Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\")).toBeDisabled();\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders the child element instead of <button> when asChild is set\", () => {\n    render(<Button asChild><a href=\"/x\">Go</a></Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Go\" })).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.queryByRole(\"button\")).not.toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "`components/auth/sign-out-control.tsx`",
        "content": "Untested: `full` prop toggles `w-full justify-center`; wraps children correctly inside Clerk's `SignOutButton`. Needs `@clerk/nextjs` mocked.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "5. Missing error-handling tests (explicit ask)",
        "content": "\n| Function | Untested failure mode |\n|---|---|\n| `listSources()` | DB row fails `sourceSchema.parse` (malformed/legacy `config` JSON) — no test proves this throws cleanly rather than returning corrupt data |\n| `requireReviewer()` | Reached with no session (proxy/handler disagreement) — the one deliberate throw path in the app, currently unverified |\n| `createSourceSchema` / `sourceConfigSchema` | No test asserts *which* field a validation error names — matters if these errors are surfaced to a form |\n| `proxy.ts` matcher | No test for a request to `/api/x` when `Authorization` header is malformed vs absent |\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "6. Integration test gaps",
        "content": "\n- **Sources page (`app/(console)/sources/page.tsx`)**: no test that it renders `SourcesEmptyState` when `listSources()` returns `[]` vs `SourceTable` when populated — this is a Server Component, needs either a Playwright test or RSC-aware test setup.\n- **Clerk appearance (`lib/clerk-appearance.ts`)**: no test/snapshot confirming no hue values sneak into `clerkAppearance.variables` (regression guard for the AGENTS.md \"no color\" rule) — a cheap regex-based unit test would catch a future contributor pasting Clerk's default blue.\n- **DB schema (`lib/db/schema.ts`)**: no migration/constraint test verifying foreign keys actually reject orphaned inserts (e.g. `conflicts.matchId` pointing to a non-existent match) — would need a real/test Postgres instance via `drizzle-kit` + a test DB.\n- **End-to-end reviewer flow**: sign-in → view sources → sign-out has no Playwright coverage at all.\n\n```ts\n// lib/clerk-appearance.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { clerkAppearance } from \"./clerk-appearance\";\n\ndescribe(\"clerkAppearance\", () => {\n  it(\"contains no hue anywhere in its color variables\", () => {\n    const hexValues = Object.entries(clerkAppearance.variables)\n      .filter(([k]) => k.toLowerCase().startsWith(\"color\"))\n      .map(([, v]) => v)\n      .filter((v): v is string => typeof v === \"string\" && v.startsWith(\"#\"));\n\n    for (const hex of hexValues) {\n      const [r, g, b] = [hex.slice(1, 3), hex.slice(3, 5), hex.slice(5, 7)].map((h) => parseInt(h, 16));\n      // Achromatic means R, G, B are equal (or the value isn't a hex at all).\n      expect(r).toBe(g);\n      expect(g).toBe(b);\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Priority order",
        "content": "1. Install Vitest + Testing Library (blocking everything).\n2. `reviewer-label.ts`, `types/source.ts` schemas, `lib/server/auth.ts` — small, high-stakes, pure/mockable.\n3. `lib/server/sources.ts`, `severity-mark.tsx`, `source-table.tsx`.\n4. Playwright for `proxy.ts` and the sign-in→console→sign-out flow — the actual security boundary has no coverage today and is the biggest real risk in this codebase.",
        "level": 2
